          %h2#Idea Idea
          %h3#general_idea General idea
          %p
            The
            %em AdS-CFT correspondence
            at its heart is the observation (
            %a{:href => "#Witten98"}> Witten 98, Section 2.4
            ) that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
            for various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            coupled to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+gravity"} Einstein gravity
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            are, when expressed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            of the
            = succeed "-values" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+functions"} generating functions
            for
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            on that
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
          %p#HolographicPrincipleInIntroduction
            This is traditionally interpreted as a concrete realization of a vague “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"}> holographic principle
            ” according to which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            spacetimes is controlled, in one way or other, by “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theories"}> boundary field theories
            ” on effective spacetime boundaries, such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizons"} event horizons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            itself was the fact that the apparent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+gravity"} Einstein gravity
            scales with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/area"} area
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizon"} event horizon
            instead of the black hole’s bulk volume (which is not even well-defined), suggesting that gravity encodes or is encoded by some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            associated with horizons; an idea that, in turn, seems to find a concrete realization in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open%2Fclosed+string+duality"} open/closed string duality
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} vicinity
            of, more generally,
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+networks"} tensor networks
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+codes"} quantum error correcting codes
          %p
            The AdS/CFT correspondence itself crucially involves the exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_{d+1}
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+group"} anti de Sitter group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+group"} conformal group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            of dimension
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            of both is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(d,2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+theory"} group theory
            underlying it, in particular in how it puts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            on the gravity side in correspondence with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sources"} sources
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            on the field theory side, respectively.
          %p
            In extrapolation of these elementary computations, the AdS/CFT correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecturally
            extends to a more general identification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/states"} states
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"}> quantum gravity
            ) on asymptotically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetimes"} anti de Sitter spacetimes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            with
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theories"} conformal field theories
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            of dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            (
            %a{:href => "#GubserKlebanovPolyakov98"}> Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov 98 (12)
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98, (2.11)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbation theory
            on one side of the correspondence relates to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbation
            on the other side.
          %p
            While this works to some extent quite generally (see e.g.
            %a{:href => "#Natsuume15"} Natsuume 15
            for review), allowing applications such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+in+condensed+matter+physics"} AdS/CFT in condensed matter physics
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/CFT in quantum chromodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1%2FN+expansion"} 1/N expansion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+field+theories"} superconformal field theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theories"}> super Yang-Mills theories
            ) on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundaries"} asymptotic boundaries
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near-horizon+limits"} near-horizon limits
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3-branes"} D3-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            to corresponding sectors of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            away from the brane.
          %p
            Before the proposal for the actual matching rule of ADS/CFT (
            %a{:href => "#GubserKlebanovPolyakov98"}> Gubser-Klebanov-Polyakov 98 (12)
            ,
