          %p
            It had already been observed by
            %a{:href => "#BDPS87"} Bergshoeff, Duff, Pope &amp; Sezgin
            and
            %a{:href => "#DuffSutton88"} Duff &amp; Sutton 1988
            (see also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Duff98"} Duff 1998
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Duff99"} Duff 1999
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+brane"} fundamental brane
            stretched over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS+spacetime"} AdS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of its own
            = succeed "-incarnation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ClausKalloshProeyen97"} Claus, Kallosh &amp; Proeyen 1997
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DGGGTT98"} DGGGTT 98
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ClausKalloshKumarTownsend98"} Claus-Kallosh, Kumar &amp; Townsend 1998
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PastiSorokinTonin99"} Pasti, Sorokin &amp; Tonin 1999
            %em
              %a{:href => "Green-Schwarz+action+functional#AsPartOfTheAdSCFTCorrespodence"} super p-brane – As part of the AdS-CFT correspondence
          %p
            More recently, for the archetypical case of AdS/CFT relating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=4 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+string+theory"} type IIB string theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} super anti-de Sitter spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi AdS
                      %mn 5
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5 \times S^5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BeisertEtAl10"} Beisert et al. 10
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Escobedo12"} Escobedo 12
            %em
              %a{:href => "#Checks"} Checks
            below.
          %p
            Thus regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open%2Fclosed+string+duality"} open/closed string duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            has two equivalent descriptions:
          %p
            1) as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            coming from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            attached to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
          %p
            2) as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            theory coming from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+strings"} closed strings
            emitted/absorbed by the brane.
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/OpenClosedCylinderWorldsheetEndingOnBranes.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "open/closed+string+duality#Schomerus07"} Schomerus 07, Figure 4
              %a{:href => "open/closed+string+duality#Peschanskia09"} Peschanskia 09, Figure 1
          %p This gives a vivid intuitive picture of the mechanism underlying the correspondence: An excitation of the gauge field on the brane goes along with an excitation of the field of gravity around the brane, and either is faithfully reflected in the other; at least in the suitable limits.
          %h3#SmallNCorrections
            Small-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            corrections
          %p
            The AdS/CFT correspondence has been widely discussed and is mostly understood by default only in the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"}
                large
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                limit
            and for large
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %p
            But it is expected (cf.
            %a{:href => "#AharonyGubserMaldacenaOoguriOz99"} AGMOO99
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9905111.pdf#page=61"} p. 60
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Chester18"} Chester 2018
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ChesterPerlmutter18"} Chester &amp; Perlmutter 2018 p. 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality
            still applies in the opposite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+1%2FN+limit"} large 1/N limit
            = succeed "-side" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative string theory
                (for small
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
            %li
              %p
                from putative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                (for the full
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+1%2FN+limit"} large 1/N limit
          %p#AdSCFTForSmallN
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
